        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12526176/comment/13126431",
          "id": "13126431",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=stillalex",
            "name": "stillalex",
            "key": "alex.parvulescu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133"
            },
            "displayName": "Alex Deparvu",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "body": "I've committed the patch with some tiny changes:\n - no hit count on the cache - I added a total access count which will be used by the other stats as well. the mechanism was already in place\n - no put count - I can't see a situation where #puts != #misses.\n - cache manager logging to debug instead on info\n - I moved the logic to build cache info in the AbstractCache class\n\nThe AbstractBundlePersistenceManager stuff will come at a later time, along with a dedicated stats object.\nDid I forget anything?\n\nps: we are back in trunk with the changes, so feel free to dive in ;)",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=stillalex",
